(186696, 10179, 1880, '<td valign="top">I really liked this photograph. It was under rated. Seniors make such incredible subjects. They have such character derived from their years. Nice job.<br/> <br/>Bob</td>', 'I really liked this photograph. It was under rated. Seniors make such incredible subjects. They have such character derived from their years. Nice job. Bob', '2003-01-09 23:33:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(186721, 10252, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club by Request<br/> <br/>I enjoyed this one during the challenge.  I like the grain.  Almost a Pointillist effect.  <br/>I think the cropping would have worked better higher from the bottom of the picture, or lower showing the mouth.  The nose leads away from the eyes, which are the highlight of the picture as it is.<br/> <br/>The left side of the frame goes a bit dark.  The eye is lost in shadow at the left edge.  Contrast is a smidge high, the ridge and tip of the nose are starting to burn out.  <br/> <br/>Focus is good, depth of field is good.  The modes eyes really make this piece, which is why I would vote for a tighter crop.  Lot of expression there.   I like the angle to the face from the camera.  I voted a 7 in the challenge, and on reflection it still holds up.  <br/> <br/>-alex</td>', 'Critique Club by Request I enjoyed this one during the challenge.  I like the grain.  Almost a Pointillist effect.  I think the cropping would have worked better higher from the bottom of the picture, or lower showing the mouth.  The nose leads away from the eyes, which are the highlight of the picture as it is. The left side of the frame goes a bit dark.  The eye is lost in shadow at the left edge.  Contrast is a smidge high, the ridge and tip of the nose are starting to burn out.   Focus is good, depth of field is good.  The modes eyes really make this piece, which is why I would vote for a tighter crop.  Lot of expression there.   I like the angle to the face from the camera.  I voted a 7 in the challenge, and on reflection it still holds up.   -alex', '2003-01-10 01:07:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(186748, 10315, 3900, '<td valign="top">How anybody could give this a ''1'' I''ll never figure out.  Obviously there are people here who simply do not care about photographic qualities, or the fact that "cats are people too." :-)  Just look at that face!!!  All I can say is "great job" and this should''ve been number one!</td>', 'How anybody could give this a ''1'' I''ll never figure out.  Obviously there are people here who simply do not care about photographic qualities, or the fact that "cats are people too." :-)  Just look at that face!!!  All I can say is "great job" and this should''ve been number one!', '2003-01-10 04:35:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(186764, 10315, 472, '<td valign="top">I think the low votes are indicative of hard-line "does not meet the challenge" opinions.  Also, believe it or not, there are people that see pets not as individuals with personalities, but more as something akin to inanimate objects.</td>', 'I think the low votes are indicative of hard-line "does not meet the challenge" opinions.  Also, believe it or not, there are people that see pets not as individuals with personalities, but more as something akin to inanimate objects.', '2003-01-10 07:40:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(186873, 10203, 724, '<td valign="top">Ha Ha, a character for sure!! Can I have this one framed?</td>', 'Ha Ha, a character for sure!! Can I have this one framed?', '2003-01-10 11:59:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(186953, 10129, 656, '<td valign="top">You requested a critique:  A good, clean, well lit black and white picture of a ornament/scuplture.  THe background is nicely dark and the off-center framing works well, with the lion''s head being tilted to ''face'' into the space.<br/> <br/>The tonal contrast on the lion is quite flat and I think could have been enhanced by less even lighting to bring out the texture and three dimensional nature of the object more strongly.  <br/> <br/>The border enhances the picture and sets it off well.  I think you really scored badly because this is more of a ''still life'' than a portrait and people voted accordingly.<br/> <br/></td>', 'You requested a critique:  A good, clean, well lit black and white picture of a ornament/scuplture.  THe background is nicely dark and the off-center framing works well, with the lion''s head being tilted to ''face'' into the space. The tonal contrast on the lion is quite flat and I think could have been enhanced by less even lighting to bring out the texture and three dimensional nature of the object more strongly.   The border enhances the picture and sets it off well.  I think you really scored badly because this is more of a ''still life'' than a portrait and people voted accordingly. ', '2003-01-10 14:40:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(187060, 10223, 3032, '<td valign="top">Just a quick comment (read the cc forum).<br/> <br/>The image is a bit on the soft side, I personally don''t like that much. The lighting of the body is okish, but the differences in lighting of the face are a bit too big, the right side is fine, but the left side has shadows that don''t look nice. Combined with the facial expression it looks (on the left) like someone who has been hit on the eye or didn''t get much rest in her sleep.<br/>The face and body language say "bored", don''t like that. (scored it a 6)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-01-10 19:22:31.</i></td>', 'Just a quick comment (read the cc forum). The image is a bit on the soft side, I personally don''t like that much. The lighting of the body is okish, but the differences in lighting of the face are a bit too big, the right side is fine, but the left side has shadows that don''t look nice. Combined with the facial expression it looks (on the left) like someone who has been hit on the eye or didn''t get much rest in her sleep.The face and body language say "bored", don''t like that. (scored it a 6)', '2003-01-10 18:02:12.000000', '2003-01-10 19:22:31.000000', 0),
(187184, 10315, 2172, '<td valign="top">Mag - This an excellent photo!  So technically clean - as usual -  and extremely emotional.  I would''ve voted it a 10, had I voted.<br/>Ruthann</td>', 'Mag - This an excellent photo!  So technically clean - as usual -  and extremely emotional.  I would''ve voted it a 10, had I voted.Ruthann', '2003-01-10 22:22:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(187222, 10117, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review by Request.<br/> <br/>I think this photo would have been stronger with more light on the subject and a different background.  The bright white of the lines on the wall make the subject look like she is in the shadows.  The highlite along the raised right forearm adds to the effect. <br/> <br/>I might have cropped a tiny bit more loosely to not cut off the sweater on the right arm near the elbow.<br/> <br/>Good detail, contrast, and depth of field.  The pose works well.  You can catch a glimpse of the subject''s personality here.  It''s also nice the way you managed to include the glasses, without glare from the lighting reflecting from them.  So often you either see bright reflections from the glasses, or a squinty subject who can''t see without them.  Overall a nice photo.</td>', 'Critique Club Review by Request. I think this photo would have been stronger with more light on the subject and a different background.  The bright white of the lines on the wall make the subject look like she is in the shadows.  The highlite along the raised right forearm adds to the effect.  I might have cropped a tiny bit more loosely to not cut off the sweater on the right arm near the elbow. Good detail, contrast, and depth of field.  The pose works well.  You can catch a glimpse of the subject''s personality here.  It''s also nice the way you managed to include the glasses, without glare from the lighting reflecting from them.  So often you either see bright reflections from the glasses, or a squinty subject who can''t see without them.  Overall a nice photo.', '2003-01-11 03:20:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(187657, 10166, 772, '<td valign="top">test critique for randomly assigned critique club photo... testing...</td>', 'test critique for randomly assigned critique club photo... testing...', '2003-01-12 17:47:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(187872, 10173, 327, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Composition/Content: here is very nice although as I said during the challenge I wish they''d been closer together. Still it can be said they look so relaxed and natural here. I don''t think the crop could be improved on, it''s wonderful as is the background.<br/> <br/>Lighting: again I will say that they seem a little dark. The pretty girl on the left is hidden in shadow while we can''t see all of the pretty girl on the right. <br/> <br/>It''s a charming shot and I like it.</td>', 'Critique Club Composition/Content: here is very nice although as I said during the challenge I wish they''d been closer together. Still it can be said they look so relaxed and natural here. I don''t think the crop could be improved on, it''s wonderful as is the background. Lighting: again I will say that they seem a little dark. The pretty girl on the left is hidden in shadow while we can''t see all of the pretty girl on the right.  It''s a charming shot and I like it.', '2003-01-12 20:51:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(193561, 10124, 1005, '<td valign="top">Although this worked out very nicely in black and white, I do like the color version just a tad better.  The yellows along it''s face are really nice!  This shot should have placed better!  It''s wonderful!</td>', 'Although this worked out very nicely in black and white, I do like the color version just a tad better.  The yellows along it''s face are really nice!  This shot should have placed better!  It''s wonderful!', '2003-01-17 15:11:27.000000', NULL, 0),
